# RUSTSEC-2026-0587 fix for host/witness-wasi-harness); >= 1.98 because 1.97's
# -C strip=debuginfo writes macOS dylibs whose string pool dyld on macOS 27
# rejects (rust-lang/rust#157750), which broke local exec-tool builds; and
# >= 1.100 for WASI exit codes (1.99's std has no exit-with-code import).
# rules_rust reads rust.toolchain ONLY from the root module, so relay must
# set it itself: without this block relay builds on rules_rust 0.70.0's
# default 1.95.0, whatever rules_wasm_component registers. edition and
# extra_target_triples are left at rules_rust's defaults (2021; the four
# linux/darwin hosts plus wasm32-unknown-unknown, -wasip1, -wasip2), as
# before. rules_rust 0.70.0 ships sha256s only up to 1.95.0; these are
# copied from rules_wasm_component (0a743a3) and checked against
# static.rust-lang.org/dist/*.sha256.
